# Spree's admin and API controllers handed the whole request `search` hash to
# the searchlogic query builder, which realises each hash key as a named-scope
# method invocation on the model and assembles the conditions and the ORDER BY
# from the caller's keys and values. An unauthenticated caller supplying
# `search[instance_eval]` reached arbitrary method dispatch through that
# key-to-method mapping, and the sort key flowed straight into SQL. The
# vulnerable form, verbatim from core/app/controllers/admin/orders_controller.rb
# `collection` at the fixed revision's parent:
#
#   params[:search][:order] ||= "descend_by_completed_at"
#   @search = Order.searchlogic(params[:search])
#   @collection = @search.do_search.paginate(:include  => [:user, :shipments, :payments],
#                                   :per_page => Spree::Config[:orders_per_page],
#                                   :page     => params[:page])
#
# The fixed revision migrates every call site to meta_search: `Order.search(params[:search])`
# with only the known keys translated into `meta_search`'s own spellings
# (`completed_at_is_not_null`, `meta_sort`), so the caller's hash keys does not
# select scopes.
#
# searchlogic carried no sink: its documented contract is exactly the one the
# Rails query-builder family binds -- "turn this hash into the search's
# SQL" -- so it joins `where`, `order`, `having`, `joins` and friends as
# code.SqlExecution at args[0]. The patched `.search` call stays unlabelled
# (meta_search's entry point is not in that family), which is what the reject
# direction pins.

test "rank1777: a request hash passed wholesale to searchlogic assembles SQL from caller-controlled keys"
  lang ruby
  expect VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  class Admin::OrdersController < ApplicationController
    def collection
      params[:search] ||= {}

      if params[:search].present?
        params[:search].delete(:completed_at_not_null)
      else
        params[:search][:completed_at_not_null] = "1"
      end

      params[:search][:order] ||= "descend_by_completed_at"
      @search = Order.searchlogic(params[:search])

      @collection = @search.do_search.paginate(:per_page => 20, :page => params[:page])
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1777: meta_search's translated sort key is not the searchlogic sink"
  lang ruby
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  class Admin::OrdersController < ApplicationController
    def collection
      params[:search] ||= {}

      if order = params[:search].delete(:order)
        params[:search][:meta_sort] = order
      else
        params[:search][:meta_sort] = 'completed_at.desc'
      end

      @search = Order.search(params[:search])

      @collection = @search.paginate(:per_page => 20, :page => params[:page])
    end
  end
  ```
